Objective: Disable or capture an enemy unit

Human infiltrators can be used to devastating effect against an unprepared opponent. Infiltrators can be trained in Training Halls. To train one click on the hall and select "Build". Note that you may have to stop one of your three Eco-Spheres to free up a Team since you have only one habitat.

Infiltrators are invisible to all mechanical units. Only other human units can detect them. However, when detected, they can be fired at by any and all.

Infiltrators are great for exploring enemy complexes, to spot targets for missile attacks, and to detect land mines. Their capabilities include "Disabling" and "Stealing" enemy units. Stealing does not work against buildings. Failing an attempt to disable or to capture, or firing his sidearm causes the infiltrator to become "detected" for the rest of the turn. 

Approach the enemy complex south of yours. Stand adjacent to an enemy mobile unit to perform the required actions. Select "Disable" same as any other unit command.

